WEBVTT

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:12.583 line:75% position:3% align:start size:30%
Ask about the day you are having.
Your focus, recorded updates and task context shape the answer.

00:00:13.383 --> 00:00:22.517 line:15% position:3% align:start size:30%
The same conversation, inside the app.
Open Otto in your workspace. A question does not change your work.

00:00:25.917 --> 00:00:36.000 line:75% position:3% align:start size:30%
Ask for the unfinished work.
Otto can show a real task list, not just describe one.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:47.667 line:15% position:3% align:start size:30%
Review the same work in-app.
The pending-task tool is available here too. Looking does not mark anything done.

00:00:51.067 --> 00:01:02.233 line:75% position:3% align:start size:30%
A timely nudge, with a direct route.
Set today’s goal opens the real planning workflow in the main app.

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:13.400 line:15% position:3% align:start size:30%
Start the plan directly in-app.
Open the same planning session, review the draft, then confirm it yourself.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:17.910 line:75% position:3% align:start size:30%
Listen while Otto stays compact.
The spoken words and the highlighted recap match. The chat panel stays closed.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.896 line:75% position:3% align:start size:30%
Software-development review across three repositories.

00:01:20.896 --> 00:01:23.286 line:75% position:3% align:start size:30%
Reviewed the cursor-pagination code

00:01:23.286 --> 00:01:28.662 line:75% position:3% align:start size:30%
Read the blocker notes and an admin work-dashboard request

00:01:28.662 --> 00:01:32.843 line:75% position:3% align:start size:30%
Checked the review queue for pending reports

00:01:32.843 --> 00:01:35.830 line:75% position:3% align:start size:30%
Opened the connect-screen implementation notes

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:37.783 line:75% position:3% align:start size:30%
Listen while Otto stays compact.
The spoken words and the highlighted recap match. The chat panel stays closed.

00:01:38.583 --> 00:01:41.741 line:15% position:3% align:start size:30%
Prefer to listen inside the app?
Open Focus and play the same recap. Stop it whenever you need to.

00:01:41.741 --> 00:01:44.728 line:15% position:3% align:start size:30%
Software-development review across three repositories.

00:01:44.728 --> 00:01:47.117 line:15% position:3% align:start size:30%
Reviewed the cursor-pagination code

00:01:47.117 --> 00:01:47.683 line:15% position:3% align:start size:30%
Read the blocker notes and an admin work-dashboard request

00:01:47.683 --> 00:01:49.200 line:15% position:3% align:start size:30%
Prefer to listen inside the app?
Open Focus and play the same recap. Stop it whenever you need to.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:58.083 line:75% position:3% align:start size:30%
Confirm the recap in place.
Confirm records your review. It does not approve a task change.

00:01:58.883 --> 00:02:08.033 line:15% position:3% align:start size:30%
Or review it in the app.
Read the source notes, then confirm the interval yourself.

00:02:11.433 --> 00:02:20.667 line:75% position:3% align:start size:30%
Make the decisions in the bubble.
Accept one change, edit new work, and skip what you do not need.

00:02:21.467 --> 00:02:31.600 line:15% position:3% align:start size:30%
The same decisions are available in-app.
Each suggestion has its own accept, edit and skip controls.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:46.617 line:75% position:3% align:start size:30%
Earlier recaps live in floating Tasks.
Scroll through Recent activity and review an older Not reviewed interval.

00:02:47.417 --> 00:02:58.650 line:15% position:3% align:start size:30%
In-app, look under Focus.
The same Recent activity stream sits below your daily goal.

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:11.483 line:75% position:3% align:start size:30%
Follow the EOD reminder.
Open EOD review takes you to the main app—not a submission from the orb.

00:03:12.283 --> 00:03:19.683 line:15% position:3% align:start size:30%
Open the report directly in-app.
Review it, submit deliberately, and keep the recorded status distinct from manager approval.
